Things are finally starting to come together for RC1.
=2D We've found a good work-around for the bug in g-i where selected lines
  in multi-select lists would not be shown. We need new versions of
  some gtk packages for that, but these have now been uploaded.
  Thanks especially to Lo=EFc Minier for his fast packaging work!
=2D The last important open TODO items were done during the past week:
  - 2.6 floppy support for i386
  - partman-auto-raid (only through preseeding)

We currently still have some blocking bugs:
=2D regression in the progress bar in the newt frontend (#391676)
=2D incorrect display for CJK languages (newt/slang: #392942/392987)
=2D keyboard support on mips SGI Indigo2 (#382983)
=2D floppies too big for powerpc (should be possible to resolve using
  new infrastructure by Sylvain Ferriol)

The release preparation page on the wiki [1] is mostly up-to-date with=20
regards to issues and TODO items before the release.
The page also lists the changes implemented since Beta 3 which will be=20
used as basis for the release notes; let me know if you miss items.


Soft freeze for commits
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
We should now stop making structural changes in the installer, but bug=20
fixing is still possible. If you have doubts if a commit is OK, please=20
contact me.
Also, please contact me before uploading if you have any doubts.


Please start testing the installer for all architectures NOW
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
All udebs with functional changes have now been uploaded, so this is an=20
excellent time to test different architectures using *daily* images!

We can now still make changes. Please don't wait until the last moment to=20
test and find out there are architecture specific issues.


Release planning
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
The schedule was becoming too complex as there are two sets of migrations=20
to testing: an initial one for current state and a final one with fixes=20
and translation updates. I have therefore split it into two separate and=20
partially overlapping schedules.
It is also somewhat optimistic, so some slippage is likely. If there is=20
slippage, is is likely to be a full week. If we switch to 2.6.18 before=20
RC1, that will also likely cause a weeks delay.

I have not planned very long periods for testing. I'd rather use RC1=20
itself for extensive testing and fix remaining issues in RC2.

INITIAL UPLOAD
=2D-------------
Now        String freeze; soft freeze for commits, bug fixing OK
16    Oct  Start migrating current udebs to testing
16-22 Oct  Architecture tests based on daily images; fix where needed !!!
20/21 Oct  First upload of debian-installer
