(Please reply to the debian-boot list.)

Preparations for Release Candidate 1 of the installer have now really=20
started. All important functional changes are now included in the daily=20
images.

In order improve the quality of the release and reduce the number of nasty=
=20
surprises afterwards, it would be great if we could get some help testing=20
the installer during *this week*.

Please make sure you use one of the _daily built_ images available from:
http://www.debian.org/devel/debian-installer/
or
http://cdimage.debian.org/cdimage/daily-builds/daily/arch-latest/

and file an installation report with your findings:
http://d-i.alioth.debian.org/manual/en.i386/ch05s03.html#submit-bug

See this wiki page for a general overview of the planned release,=20
including known issues:
http://wiki.debian.org/DebianInstaller/EtchRC1Prep


Testing the installer for your favorite architecture(s)
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
This is the main focus for this call for testing. Please let us know if=20
there are any important issues, especially regressions from previous=20
releases. If you can, try different installation methods.

Note that the installer still uses 2.6.17. Main reason is that 2.6.18 is=20
not yet ready to migrate to testing and switching to 2.6.18 would=20
therefore block RC1 of d-i. Depending on the kernel team and RMs, we may=20
still switch to 2.6.18 before RC1, but switching immediately afterwards=20
looks more likely.

Other things to test
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
There is a number of other things that could be tested, mostly new=20
functionality that was added recently:
=2D graphical installer, especially whether your mouse and touchpad work
  correctly
=2D crypto support in partman: the installer now has crypto support both
  for guided [1] and manual [2] partitioning; thorough tests, including
  of the actual security of the installed system, very, very welcome
=2D automatic raid partitioning (preseeded only [1])
=2D 2.6 based installation floppies for i386
=2D support for non-standard filesystems (i.e. anything other than ext3)
=2D if you speak a language other than English, consider installing in
  that language; note that one last round of translation updates is
  still planned, but reports of issues are still appreciated

TIA,
=46rans Pop

[1]http://d-i.alioth.debian.org/manual/en.i386/ch06s03.html#di-partition
[2]http://d-i.alioth.debian.org/manual/en.i386/ch06s03.html#partman-crypto
[3]http://d-i.alioth.debian.org/manual/en.i386/apbs04.html#preseed-partman-=
raid

